\n&= 2x - 2 + 3 \\\\\n&= 2x + 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we just take the expression for $f$ and replace every occurrence of $x$ with the expression for $g(x)$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185381 #edb/ref 1065 9264 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185381 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "7eaa8bd9-f7a4-5d70-b5f6-8cb47bd3a7bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185381 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542626 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186543600 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542626 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186543609 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542626 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186543653 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542626 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542626 #edb/ref 1045 "Describing Function Composition" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542626 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186543609 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542626 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542626 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542626 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "a7028d09-7fe3-5f85-985d-69463f19127c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542682 #edb/ref 1080 "2{a}^{2}+2a+4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542682 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542682 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "11b1c1bf-2a67-5c91-92bc-0b92c34f4a40" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542776 #edb/ref 1080 "4{p}^{2}+4p-5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542776 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542776 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "32a224a7-1eb4-5777-a6ac-6be22859d307" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542845 #edb/ref 1080 "4{p}^{2}-6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542845 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542845 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4a7f8e06-5a54-5672-ba21-201d8162c811" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542849 #edb/ref 1080 "{a}^{2}+2a-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542849 #edb/r